@page "/docs/theming/themes"

@* Setting the app's look with IzzyTheme: preset, brand, grays, radius, density, fonts. From
   docs/styling.md ("Presets and colors", "Customizing"); values checked against ThemeValues.cs. *@

<ArticlePage Section="theming" Slug="themes">
    <Lead>
        <Code>IzzyTheme</Code> sets the whole app's look in one place, in <Code>App.razor</Code>'s <Code>head</Code>. It
        sets a preset, then your brand color, grays, radius, density and fonts over it. It renders on the server, so the
        theme applies on first paint, in every render mode and with JavaScript off.
    </Lead>
    <ChildContent>
        <Heading Level="2">Set the theme</Heading>
        <TextBlock>Put one <Code>IzzyTheme</Code> in the <Code>head</Code>, after the stylesheet:</TextBlock>
        <Code Block Language="razor" Title="Components/App.razor">@SetTheme</Code>
        <TextBlock>
            A parameter you set overrides the preset's value; one you leave unset keeps it. With no parameters at all, you
            get the Standard preset, in blue on neutral grays.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Presets</Heading>
        <TextBlock>A preset is a starting set of defaults: the density, shape, type and colors that suit a kind of app. Set <Code>Preset</Code> to choose one.</TextBlock>
        <ExampleViewer Example="izzy-theme-presets" />
        <TextBlock>Each card in this example themes part of a page. There, a preset doesn't bring its brand and gray, so each card sets them too. Fonts are app-wide, so Editorial's fonts don't show here.</TextBlock>
        <Prose Class="site-table ib-scroll">
            <table>
                <thead><tr><th>Preset</th><th>For</th><th>Controls</th><th>Shape</th><th>Type</th><th>Brand</th><th>Gray</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td><code>Standard</code></td><td>Internal tools, line-of-business</td><td>36px</td><td>Medium radius, hairline shadow</td><td>Inter</td><td>Blue</td><td>Neutral</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>Compact</code></td><td>Admin, ERP, finance, data grids</td><td>32px, tight rows</td><td>Small radius, borders only</td><td>Inter</td><td>Indigo</td><td>Slate</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>Soft</code></td><td>Consumer apps, education, health</td><td>40px, roomy</td><td>Large radius, gentle shadow</td><td>Inter</td><td>Teal</td><td>Neutral</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>Editorial</code></td><td>Docs, publishing, knowledge bases</td><td>36px</td><td>Large radius</td><td>IBM Plex Sans, Newsreader headings</td><td>Ink</td><td>Stone</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </Prose>
        <TextBlock>Editorial's fonts don't ship with IzzyBlazor. Load them yourself, as shown under <Anchor Href="docs/theming/themes#fonts">Fonts</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Your brand color</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            The brand color is the primary accent. It colors primary buttons, links, focus rings, the soft ring around a
            focused field, selected rows, switches and sliders. Set <Code>Brand</Code> to a hex color, or to the name of a
            built-in one.
        </TextBlock>
        <ExampleViewer Example="izzy-theme-brands" />
        <TextBlock>
            From a hex color, IzzyBlazor works out four shades, in light and dark: the fill, the text on it, the color as
            text and a soft tint. Each is checked for contrast. In light mode the fill is your color, unless no text can
            reach 4.5:1 on it; then only its lightness changes. In dark mode, a dark color is lightened so controls still
            show. To set the shades yourself, see
            <Anchor Href="docs/theming/tokens#brand-shades-by-hand">Brand shades by hand</Anchor>.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Grays</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            The grays color the page, surfaces, fills, borders and text. Set <Code>Gray</Code> to <Code>neutral</Code> (the
            default), <Code>slate</Code> (cool) or <Code>stone</Code> (warm, for serif headings). Or set it to a hex color
            for your light page.
        </TextBlock>
        <TextBlock>
            From a hex color, the surfaces, fills, borders and text are worked out in its hue, with the text checked for
            contrast. A dark set is made to match. A very light or dark page color is kept light enough for text to read.
        </TextBlock>
        <Code Block Language="razor">@Grays</Code>

        <Heading Level="2">Radius and density</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            To round every corner in proportion, set <Code>Radius</Code>: <Code>None</Code>, <Code>Sm</Code>,
            <Code>Md</Code> (the default), <Code>Lg</Code>, or <Code>Full</Code> for pill-shaped controls.
        </TextBlock>
        <TextBlock>
            Density sets control heights, table rows and card padding. Set <Code>Density</Code> to <Code>Compact</Code>
            (32px controls), <Code>Standard</Code> (36px) or <Code>Comfortable</Code> (40px).
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Fonts</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            Body text is Inter, which ships with IzzyBlazor. Browsers download only the character sets a page uses, and
            nothing once you name another font. IzzyTheme preloads Inter's Latin set, so text doesn't paint in a fallback
            font first; name another body font with <Code>BodyFont</Code>, not in CSS, so Inter isn't preloaded for
            nothing. To use your own fonts, set <Code>BodyFont</Code>, <Code>HeadingFont</Code>
            and <Code>MonoFont</Code>. To change the headings' weight, set <Code>HeadingWeight</Code>. Load any font other
            than Inter yourself:
        </TextBlock>
        <Code Block Language="razor">@Fonts</Code>
        <TextBlock>The Editorial preset uses IBM Plex Sans and Newsreader:</TextBlock>
        <Code Block Language="razor">@EditorialFonts</Code>

        <Heading Level="2">App-wide or part of a page</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            Fonts, <Code>HeadingWeight</Code>, a hex <Code>Gray</Code> and <Code>Scrollbars</Code> are app-wide. Set them on
            the <Code>IzzyTheme</Code> in the <Code>head</Code>. <Code>Scrollbars</Code> sets whether the page's own
            scrollbar is themed too. The other parameters also work on part of a page, on a <Anchor Href="docs/components/theme-scope">ThemeScope</Anchor>; see <Anchor Href="docs/theming/tokens#theme-part-of-a-page">Theme part of a page</Anchor>.
        </TextBlock>
        <TextBlock>
            <Code>IzzyTheme</Code> writes hex colors and fonts in a small <Code>style</Code> block. For a strict
            Content-Security-Policy, pass your nonce as <Code>Nonce</Code>.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Next steps</Heading>
        <List Gap="2">
            <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/theming/color-scheme">Light and dark</Anchor>: the default scheme and a switch for users.</ListItem>
            <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/theming/tokens">Tokens and customizing</Anchor>: exact values with CSS variables.</ListItem>
            <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/components/izzy-theme/api">IzzyTheme API</Anchor>: every parameter.</ListItem>
        </List>
    </ChildContent>
</ArticlePage>

@code {
    private const string SetTheme = """
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["_content/IzzyBlazor.Core/izzyblazor.css"]" />
        <IzzyTheme Preset="ThemePreset.Soft" Brand="#0a7d5a" Radius="ThemeRadius.Full" />
        """;

    private const string Grays = """
        <IzzyTheme Gray="slate" />
        @* or your light page color; app-wide *@
        <IzzyTheme Gray="#f4efe6" />
        """;

    private const string EditorialFonts = """
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600&family=Newsreader:opsz,wght@6..72,500..600&display=swap" />
        """;

    private const string Fonts = """
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Sora:wght@400;600;700&display=swap" />
        <IzzyTheme BodyFont="Sora, system-ui, sans-serif" HeadingWeight="700" />
        """;
}
